      "dom_id": "question-35926",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic paraboloid $12z=4(x+2)^{2}-3{y}^{2}$ and the plane \n$z=1$  onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=1$, we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12z & =4(x+2)^{2}-3{y}^{2} \\\\ 12(1) & =4(x+2)^{2}-3{y}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =4(x+2)^{2}-3{y}^{2} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{3}$ and $2.$",
