      "dom_id": "question-72302",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the hyperbolic paraboloid $(x-6)^{2}-8(y+2)^{2}=z+4$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $x=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-6)^{2}-8(y+2)^{2} & =0+4 \\\\ 36-8(y+2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ 32 & =8(y+2)^{2} \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y+2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =-2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $y=-4$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-4,0)$ and $(0,0,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
